## 2. System Architecture

The application operates on a decoupled, microservice-augmented modular monolith design to ensure high availability and strict separation of concerns.

```mermaid
graph TD
    User([End User / Web Client])
    Gateway[Next.js Web Server / PWA]
    API[NestJS API Gateway]
    AI[FastAPI Python Microservice]
    DB[(PostgreSQL + TimescaleDB)]
    
    User -->|HTTPS / WSS| Gateway
    Gateway -->|GraphQL / REST / JWT| API
    
    subgraph "Core NestJS ERP Gateway"
      Auth[AuthModule & RBAC]
      Tenant[Tenant Middleware]
      Audit[Audit Interceptor]
      
      API --> Auth
      Auth --> Tenant
      Tenant --> Audit
    end

    Audit -->|HTTP POST| AI
    Audit -->|Prisma Client| DB
    
    subgraph "Data Persistence"
      DB_RLS[Postgres Row-Level Security]
      DB --> DB_RLS
    end
```

### Key Technologies:
* **Frontend:** Next.js with Progressive Web App (PWA) capabilities for offline read-access to critical reports.
* **Backend:** NestJS API Gateway handling complex business logic, Role-Based Access Control (RBAC), and tenant routing.
* **AI/ML:** FastAPI (Python) running Facebook Prophet for deterministic time-series forecasting.
* **Database:** PostgreSQL accelerated by TimescaleDB for high-volume time-series ledger transactions.
* **ORM:** Prisma Client with dynamic Row-Level Security (RLS) extensions.

